  "critical": false,
  "description": "Circuit-level design pedagogy for DC-to-AC inverters using switching topologies. Covers the H-bridge (four switches arranged in an H), square-wave and SPWM (sinusoidal pulse-width modulation) synthesis, dead-time insertion to prevent shoot-through, MOSFET vs IGBT device selection, and LC output filtering to remove switching harmonics. Owns the circuit DESIGN; system-level inverter manufacturing and grid-tie applications are covered by power-electronics.",
  "early_win": false,
